## Releasing

Releases are published to PyPI with
[Trusted Publishing](https://docs.pypi.org/trusted-publishers/), so no API
tokens or secrets are stored in this repository.

**One-time setup**: at <https://pypi.org/manage/account/publishing/>, register a
publisher with owner `{{ github_username }}`, repository `{{ github_repo }}`,
workflow `publish.yml` and environment `pypi`.

Then, to release:

```bash
uv version --bump patch    # or minor / major
git commit -am "Release v$(uv version --short)"
git tag "v$(uv version --short)"
git push --follow-tags
```

The publish workflow verifies that the tag matches the project version, builds
the distributions, uploads them to PyPI with Sigstore attestations, and creates
a GitHub release.

